  "result": "All seven tests pass, across both test files.\n\n**What changed in `editor/buffer.py`**\n\n- **Unified edit command.** The record now stores `pos`, `old`, and `new` text. Insert has empty old text, delete has empty new text, and replace has both. Inverting an edit just swaps old and new, so every operation is one undo step.\n- **`replace(pos, n, s)`** validates the range, captures the removed text, and applies one command. Undo restores the original slice and redo reapplies the replacement.\n- **`history_len()`** returns the size of the undo stack.\n- **`undo_all()`** calls undo until it returns false. Each step lands on the redo stack in order, so redo replays them one at a time.\n- **Shared bounds check.** Insert, delete, and replace now use one range validator that rejects negative positions, negative lengths, and ranges past the end.\n\n```\npython -m pytest -q\n7 passed in 0.03s\n```",
